    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a high-ceiling core, anchored by **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (79.96) and **Yordan Alvarez** (75.99). **Pete Crow-Armstrong** stands out as our most efficient play, capitalizing on a generous 4.97 xERA matchup against Arrighetti and, crucially, an elite 88% stolen base opportunity window against a slow-delivering pitcher. While he faces a slight penalty for an #8 spot in the order and a wind-in risk, his speed profile makes him a must-start in our pursuit of category scarcity. Similarly, **Yordan Alvarez** remains locked into the core, offering elite xwOBA metrics that easily overcome a moderate wind-in warning to provide a high floor for HR and RBI production.\n\nAmong our mid-tier starts, **Colt Keith** (68.51) and **Trea Turner** (67.75) benefit significantly from lead-off roles and favorable park factors, while **Junior Caminero** (67.43) remains a high-upside play despite the daunting task of facing Gerrit Cole. The most interesting bench decision involved **Caleb Durbin** (43.68), who nearly cracked the lineup due to his sprint speed profile. However, **Caleb Durbin** fell just short of the efficiency threshold as his projected #9 spot and a difficult matchup against Connor Prielipp (3.44 xERA) suppressed his scoring potential compared to the rest of the utility corps.\n\nWe must remain vigilant regarding our \"Lineup Pending\" designations, as **Dillon Dingler**, **Gary Sanchez**, **Luke Raley**, **Colt Keith**, **Trea Turner**, **Casey Schmitt**, **Kazuma Okamoto**, **Kyle Schwarber**, **Carson Benge**, **Christian Yelich**, and **Junior Caminero** are all subject to final confirmation. **Christian Yelich** presents a distinct risk today; his score (44.82) is heavily dampened by a 3.50 xERA matchup and a negative platoon split, though we are tracking his start solely because his 85% SB opportunity against a slow-delivery pitcher provides essential value in our scarcest category. Outside of the active roster, **Zac Veen** remains sidelined in Albuquerque, and we continue to monitor the status of depth pieces like **Lars Nootbaar**, **Josh Smith**, **Chase Meidroth**, **Luis Pena**, and **Pedro Ramirez** for potential rotation adjustments if weather or lineup shuffling impacts our primary starters.",
